# Vambrace Adventure — Project Libraries

This directory contains the private libraries for the Vambrace firmware.
PlatformIO compiles them as static libraries and links them into the final executable.

Each library lives in its own subdirectory with a `.hpp`/`.cpp` pair.

---

## Current Structure

```plaintext
lib/
├── vambrace_app/
│   ├── vambrace_app.hpp      # TeleoperationCmd class and associated structs
│   └── vambrace_app.cpp      # Setters and getters implementation
│
├── vambrace_ros/
│   ├── vambrace_ros.hpp      # Public function declarations for the ROS layer
│   └── vambrace_ros.cpp      # Init, publish and spin over WiFi UDP
│
├── vambrace_config/
│   └── vambrace_config.hpp   # ROS 2 topic names, status LED pin
│
├── vambrace_secret/
│   ├── vambrace_secret.hpp      # SSID, password, agent IP and port (gitignored)
│   └── vambrace_secret_ex.hpp   # Example template for new contributors
│
└── README                    # This file
```

---

## Library Responsibilities

### `vambrace_app` — Teleoperation Data Model

- Defines all data the bracelet can send to ORION.
- No hardware or ROS dependencies — testable in native environment.

  - **Structs:** `MobileBaseVelocity`, `ArmPosition`
  - **Core class:** `TeleoperationCmd`

### `vambrace_ros` — micro-ROS Communication Layer

- Connects the ESP32 to the micro-ROS agent via WiFi UDP.
- Initializes the ROS 2 node and 5 publishers.
- Publishes `TeleoperationCmd` data on every loop cycle.

- **Depends on:** `vambrace_app`, `vambrace_config`, `vambrace_secret`

### `vambrace_config` — Configuration Constants

- Centralizes topic names and configuration constants.
- Never hardcode these values in any other file.

### `vambrace_secret` — Network Credentials

> **NEVER** commit `vambrace_secret.hpp` — it is listed in `.gitignore`.

- To configure: copy `vambrace_secret_ex.hpp` → `vambrace_secret.hpp` and fill in your actual network credentials.

---

## Published Topics (verified against ORION)

| Topic | Type |
| --- | --- |
| `/mobile_base_controller/cmd_vel` | `geometry_msgs/msg/TwistStamped` |
| `/simple_left_arm_controller/cmd` | `std_msgs/msg/Float64MultiArray` |
| `/simple_right_arm_controller/cmd` | `std_msgs/msg/Float64MultiArray` |
| `/emotion/int` | `std_msgs/msg/Int32` |
| `/orion_response` | `std_msgs/msg/String` |

